Task 1 — Install and Initialize Vault — 20 Marks
Step 1: Check Ubuntu
Open Terminal:
lsb_release -a
Then:
uname -m
You should see something like:
x86_64
Step 2: Install required packages
sudo apt update
sudo apt install -y gpg wget curl
Step 3: Add HashiCorp repository
wget -O- https://apt.releases.hashicorp.com/gpg | \
gpg --dearmor | \
sudo tee /usr/share/keyrings/hashicorp-archive-keyring.gpg > /dev/null
Then:
echo "deb [signed-by=/usr/share/keyrings/hashicorp-archive-keyring.gpg] \
https://apt.releases.hashicorp.com $(lsb_release -cs) main" | \
sudo tee /etc/apt/sources.list.d/hashicorp.list
Update:
sudo apt update
Step 4: Install Vault
sudo apt install -y vault
Check:
vault version
You should get something similar to:
Vault v1.x.x
📸 Screenshot 1
Take a screenshot showing:
vault version
This is your Installation screenshot.
Step 5: Create Vault configuration
Create the configuration directory:
sudo mkdir -p /etc/vault.d
Create the data directory:
sudo mkdir -p /opt/vault/data
Create the configuration:
sudo nano /etc/vault.d/vault.hcl
Paste:
ui = true

storage "file" {
  path = "/opt/vault/data"
}

listener "tcp" {
  address     = "127.0.0.1:8200"
  tls_disable = true
}

api_addr = "http://127.0.0.1:8200"
Save:
Ctrl + O → Enter → Ctrl + X
8200 is Vault's port. Your Jenkins is on 8080, so there is no conflict.
Step 6: Start Vault
For your assessment, you can run:
sudo vault server -config=/etc/vault.d/vault.hcl
Keep this terminal open.
You should see Vault server logs.
Open another terminal.
Step 7: Configure Vault CLI
In the second terminal:
export VAULT_ADDR='http://127.0.0.1:8200'
Check:
echo $VAULT_ADDR
Then:
vault status
Initially you should see:
Initialized     false
Sealed          true
Step 8: Initialize Vault
Run:
vault operator init
You will get output similar to:
Unseal Key 1: xxxxxxxxx
Unseal Key 2: xxxxxxxxx
Unseal Key 3: xxxxxxxxx
Unseal Key 4: xxxxxxxxx
Unseal Key 5: xxxxxxxxx

Initial Root Token: hvs.xxxxxxxxx
⚠️ VERY IMPORTANT
Save these values somewhere safe.
Especially:
Unseal Key 1
Unseal Key 2
Unseal Key 3
Unseal Key 4
Unseal Key 5
Initial Root Token
Do not put these real values into GitHub.
Vault's default initialization uses Shamir secret sharing, where multiple key shares are generated and a threshold is required to unseal Vault. �
